  "notes": [
    "Requirements-only plan. Source calculations are obligations to implement, not evidence of executed TypeSpec, API rules, runtime validation or human acceptance.",
    "DAT 00-3: NOTE:  Certain Federal assistance programs require additional computations to arrive at the Federal share of project costs eligible for participation.  If such is the case, you will be notified.",
    "DAT 00-0 burden statement: Clicking displays burden statement: \nSF-424C Budget Information – Construction Programs Form (4040-0008)\n\nAccording to the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995, an agency may not conduct or sponsor, and a person is not required to respond to a collection of information unless it displays a valid OMB control number.  The valid OMB control number for this information collection is 4040-0008.  The time required to complete this information collection is estimated to average 2 hours per response, including the time to review instructions, search existing data resources, gather the data needed and complete and review the information collection.  If you have comments concerning the accuracy of the time estimate(s) or suggestions for improving this form, please write to:  U.S. Department of Health & Human Services, OS/OCIO/PRA, 200 Independence Ave., S.W., Suite 537-H, Washington D.C. 20201,  Attention: PRA Reports Clearance Officer.\n\nAgency       Total             Average Burden   Total Burden\n                  Responses    per response in    Hours\n                                      Hours\n\nVA              179              15/60                   45\nDOI             1274            49/60                  1046\nUSDA          934             3                         2802\nDOC            567             15/60                  142\nDOT            1650            3                         4950\nDHS            73               4                         292\nTotal            4677           9277\n\n9277 total hrs. / 4677 total responses = 2 hours per response",
    "DAT 00-4 through 00-7 supply the cost classification and a/b/c column headings. Explicit field labels repeat that context so amounts remain understandable outside the PDF table. Value-pinned label differences are recorded in the parity register.",
    "DAT 17-3 supplies percent units; 17-2 is a percentage, not a currency amount. DAT 17-1 is preserved as federal-funding section help.",
    "Answer paths follow existing SGG at 76d44680cd92a3abe648e592b04972bc5424df17. Currency samples use decimal strings; numeric constraints describe source amounts, not a claim that a JSON numeric keyword validates a string. Existing SGG federal_funding.total_project_costs is a calculated repeat of line16c, not an additional source answer; its legacy projection remains an implementation obligation.",
    "DAT Validation Message — literal source obligations for implementation review (grouped by identical text):\n\n01-c: Total Allowable Cost for 1. Administrative and Legal Expenses is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n02-c: Total Allowable Cost for 2. Land, Structures, Rights-of-way, Appraisals, Etc. is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n03-c: Total Allowable Cost for 3. Relocation Expenses and Payments is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n04-c: Total Allowable Cost for 4. Architectural and Engineering Fees is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n05-c: Total Allowable Cost for 5. Other Architectural and Engineering Fees is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n06-c: Total Allowable Cost for 6. Project and Inspection Fees is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n07-c: Total Allowable Cost for 7. Site Work is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n08-c: Total Allowable Cost for 8. Demolition and Removal is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n09-c: Total Allowable Cost for 9. Construction is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n10-c: Total Allowable Cost for 10. Equipment is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n11-c: Total Allowable Cost for 11. Miscellaneous is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n12-c: Total Allowable Cost for 12. Subtotal (Sum of Lines 1-11) is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n13-c: Total Allowable Cost for 13. Contingencies is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n14-c: Total Allowable Cost for 14. Subtotal is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n15-c: Total Allowable Cost for 15. Project (Program) Income is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n16-a: Total Cost for 16. Total Project Costs (Subtract #15 from #14) is invalid: Total Cost cannot be negative.\n\n16-b: Cost Not Allowable for Participation for 16. Total Project Costs (Subtract #15 from #14) is invalid: Cost Not Allowable for Participation cannot be negative.\n\n16-c: Total Allowable Cost for 16. Total Project Costs (Subtract #15 from #14) is invalid: Total Allowable Cost cannot be negative.\n\n17-2: Invalid Federal percentage share: Consult Federal agency for Federal percentage share\n\n17-4: Federal Funding Share is invalid: Federal Funding Share cannot be negative.",
    "DAT 17-2 has INTEGER data type and XSD FederalFundingPercentageShareValue restricts xs:int to 0–100. Preserve whole-percent entry. The instruction to consult the Federal agency identifies policy ownership; it does not specify pre-population or an authentication mechanism.",
    "Wire metadata is not an applicant question: the XSD root SF424C_2_0 requires fixed programType Construction and fixed FormVersion 2.0. Preserve these document attributes during later serialization."
